Intuitively, to maximize the number of pairs, we should use the smallest elements as the "top" mochi (the ones on top) because they are easier to satisfy the condition $x_{top} \le x_{bottom} / 2$.
Specifically, if we use a very small element as the bottom, it restricts the top element to be very small. If we use a large element as the bottom, it allows a wider range of top elements.
