Since the array is sorted, if we pick a pair $(A_i, B_j)$ with $i < j$, then $A_i \le A_j$. The condition $A_i \le B_j / 2$ implies $A_i \le A_j / 2$. If $i > j$, then $A_i \ge A_j$, so $A_i \le A_j / 2$ would imply $A_j \le A_j / 2$, which means $A_j \le 0$, but sizes are positive. Thus, we must always pick the smaller element as the top and the larger element as the bottom. So we are looking for pairs $(A_i, A_j)$ with $i < j$ such that $A_i \le A_j / 2$.

